Yeah, I remember first year Philosophy in Continuing Education.  I suspect there 
is a point buried here, but it got lost in the bu'sh' somewhere.  We are dealing 
with a language, a product of human cognition, and so, anything beyond that 
level of analysis is irrelevant to the project.  The fact that what I call a 
wall is "99.9R% empty space" does not interest me since it still stops my hand 
(also 99.9R% empty space), and it is the latter I mean by "solid".  And that is 
all that concerns us here.  

Mereology is different from set theory (different axioms at least); how the 
latter is ontological is not clear (probably because the adjective is misused in 
so many ways).  

As noted elsewhere, the part/whole relation is independent of predication.  If 
some feature carries upward or downward, that is a property of that feature, not 
of jest.It may be that being a brain or braining carries upward, so rhinoceroses 
brain.  It may be that consciousness carries downward, so that a person's brain 
is conscious.  But these moves do not apply generally (nor even here, I think -- 
but that's just me) and so are not built into Lojban or the underlying logic of 
Lojban.  In most cases where there is some carry, there is also some limitation: 
we don't (usually) go from my consciousness to the consciousness of the universe 
or even the Earth, nor to that of quarks or whatever.  

Another point that may be in here is that words are ambiguous (surprise!), even 
Lojban words.  Also vague.  The brain is the jelly in the head, but two 
different people may delimit that jelly differently, with resulting confusion 
should they meet.  Lojban does have, however, easy ways to patch up each 
individual problem, if the need arises.  More than that we cannot ask of a 
language.




